From bfa53a2ec15d7f747be511d60226631d35a3808c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild Idler Patch <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:15:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix cross-monitor resize reset, refresh project brief
 numbers, full checkAll audit

- Menu window losing its remembered custom size on a cross-monitor move
  (direct report). Root cause: win.on('resized', ...) persisted every
  native resize event unconditionally, with no way to distinguish a
  genuine manual drag from Windows' own DPI rescale, which fires a real
  'resize' event whenever the window crosses onto a display running at a
  different display-scaling percentage. Fixed with a short-lived
  suppression flag: a new 'moved' handler tracks the window's current
  display id, arms a 500ms suppression window the instant it detects a
  change, and the resize handler skips persisting (without touching the
  window's actual on-screen bounds) if that flag is set. Verified the
  compiled bundle contains the fix, and separately re-implemented the
  exact state machine standalone against a fake clock to confirm the
  decision logic across 5 scenarios (normal resize, suppressed
  OS-rescale, real resize after the guard window closes, same-display
  moves never suppressing, and no accidental re-arming).

- guild-idler-project-brief.md's content-scope line was stale ('~400
  quests... raids across 3 difficulties... achievements (leaderboards
  planned)') -- corrected to the real numbers (29 quest chains, 8 raids,
  65 achievements) with a note pointing back at the live JSON as the
  source of truth.

- Full checkAll audit across every engine.ts mutator, not just the 8
  spot-fixed last round. Script-identified 31 candidates (saveNow() +
  direct state mutation + no reportAchievements/reportGuidance); 30
  reviewed and confirmed harmless, one real gap found and fixed:
  testAddPet (a testing-tool method) mutates state.pets directly --
  exactly what FIRST_PET_HATCHED/ALL_PETS_COLLECTED check -- but never
  called checkAll, so using it to verify ALL_PETS_COLLECTED wouldn't
  have actually shown the achievement unlocking.

guild-idler-status.md updated: all three items logged/ticked off in the
Steam-launch completeness backlog. Full tsc --noEmit and vite build both
pass clean.
